#@ readme_auth
A bearer token, the one the service's own web app sends in its `Authorization` header. Get it into
the credential store with `catalog-sync login {{name}} --paste-curl -` (copy any authenticated API
call from the browser's network tab with "Copy as cURL (bash)", paste, Ctrl-D) or, once the
selectors in `credentials.py` match the real login page, `catalog-sync login {{name}} --browser`
(`--headed` when the service wants a person: a captcha, a code). The token's expiry is read from it
when it is a JWT; `catalog-sync auth status {{name}}` says how long it has.
